# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# FIRE and gradient descent are jax_md.minimize. L-BFGS is jaxopt.LBFGS or optax.lbfgs.
# The potential is the harness potential. A rejected over-long L-BFGS trial is not a call.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the problem stop, and Hessian index 0.
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD are omitted: the problem file has no per-start reference.
# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# JAX MD 0.2.29 fire_descent at the library defaults: dt_start 0.1, dt_max 0.4, n_min 5, f_inc 1.1, f_dec 0.5, alpha_start 0.1, f_alpha 0.99. The shift scales a trial so the largest per-atom move is 0.2, the ASE FIRE constructor maxstep. The potential is the harness potential for this problem. The stop is the problem force norm and the budget is the force-call cap. Gaussian force noise uses the problem seed, kappa, and clean-energy window. The Hessian is the clean force.
